1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,435
You found a nice desk organizer online, free to download.

2
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:07,080
But business cards don't fit in its drawers, and you'd like a third one.

3
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:15,374
Today I'll show you how to turn that 3D print file into a real, adjustable model with SOMA AI, and then change it the way you need.

4
00:00:15,374 --> 00:00:16,720
No CAD knowledge needed.

5
00:00:25,373 --> 00:00:26,142
We use SOMA.

6
00:00:26,142 --> 00:00:30,372
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

7
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,794
SOMA itself is free.

8
00:00:32,794 --> 00:00:35,369
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

9
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:38,092
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

10
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:41,073
Here is the part:

11
00:00:41,073 --> 00:00:44,569
a desk organizer by GummieGecko, shared on Printables.

12
00:00:47,206 --> 00:00:50,174
Two drawers in front, a deep cup for pens at the back.

13
00:00:50,174 --> 00:00:54,296
I'd like to keep business cards in the drawers, and I need one more drawer.

14
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,791
The license is Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike.

15
00:00:58,791 --> 00:01:04,050
So we may change it, as long as we credit the author and share our version under the same license.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,013
There's one file to download:

17
00:01:07,013 --> 00:01:09,096
a 3MF, the format slicers use.

18
00:01:09,096 --> 00:01:10,970
An STL works just the same.

19
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:18,571
In SOMA, I start a new model called Desk organizer, click Import, and pick the downloaded file.

20
00:01:18,571 --> 00:01:22,010
It goes into the inputs folder, where SOMA AI can use it.

21
00:01:25,173 --> 00:01:27,629
Click the file, and SOMA shows it in the viewer:

22
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:30,903
the body and the two drawers, laid out the way they are printed.

23
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:35,462
Switch on the wireframe, and you see what this file really is:

24
00:01:35,462 --> 00:01:36,842
a mesh of flat triangles.

25
00:01:36,842 --> 00:01:40,650
There's no width to change and no wall thickness, just corner points.

26
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:46,575
And the drawers are small:

27
00:01:46,575 --> 00:01:49,550
inside, they are 58 by 57 millimeters.

28
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:53,230
A business card is 85 by 55, so it won't go in.

29
00:01:54,373 --> 00:01:57,863
So instead of pushing triangles around, we let SOMA AI rebuild it.

30
00:01:59,907 --> 00:02:01,511
I click the SOMA AI tab.

31
00:02:01,511 --> 00:02:03,717
Here I just describe what I want.

32
00:02:10,507 --> 00:02:16,717
Then I pick the model, GPT-6.1 Sol, and set the effort to High, so it thinks things through.

33
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,654
Then I simply say what I want, in plain words:

34
00:02:22,654 --> 00:02:29,530
rebuild the organizer as a parametric model, with the drawers in place, and keep the original as a see-through reference.

35
00:02:32,773 --> 00:02:37,993
SOMA AI opens the file, finds the three parts, and measures the walls, the slots and the drawers.

36
00:02:37,993 --> 00:02:42,406
Then it builds them as a real model, and checks that the drawers slide out freely.

37
00:02:43,356 --> 00:02:43,701
Done:

38
00:02:43,701 --> 00:02:49,361
the body and the two drawers, at the original size of 65 by 125 by 95 millimeters.

39
00:02:49,361 --> 00:02:54,606
The structure tree lists the new parts, and the original ones as references.

40
00:02:55,556 --> 00:02:58,267
The original sits in the same place, see-through.

41
00:02:58,267 --> 00:02:59,540
Hide it, show it again:

42
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:01,366
the rebuild matches the download.

43
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:10,170
In the Parameters tab are the sizes SOMA AI made adjustable.

44
00:03:13,306 --> 00:03:16,709
Drag a slider, and the model rebuilds within seconds.

45
00:03:16,709 --> 00:03:19,470
Here the width, and here the drawer height.

46
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:22,295
The drawers and their slots change together.

47
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,550
Reset all brings the sizes back.

48
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:39,132
Now the drawers should take business cards, 85 by 55 millimeters.

49
00:03:39,132 --> 00:03:43,043
I tell SOMA AI, and ask it to show a card in each drawer.

50
00:03:47,706 --> 00:03:52,505
SOMA AI works out how big the drawers have to be inside, and makes the body just wide enough.

51
00:03:52,505 --> 00:03:55,756
Then it builds it, and checks that the drawers still slide out.

52
00:03:56,706 --> 00:03:59,493
The organizer is now 96 millimeters wide.

53
00:03:59,493 --> 00:04:02,485
Each drawer has 89 by 59 millimeters inside:

54
00:04:02,485 --> 00:04:05,068
two millimeters of room around a card.

55
00:04:05,068 --> 00:04:06,836
The height stays the same.

56
00:04:08,772 --> 00:04:10,998
To look inside, I use the Section tool.

57
00:04:10,998 --> 00:04:14,422
It only cuts open the view, the model itself doesn't change.

58
00:04:17,606 --> 00:04:20,891
There's the green card, lying flat in the upper drawer.

59
00:04:20,891 --> 00:04:23,042
The amber outline is the old drawer:

60
00:04:23,042 --> 00:04:24,296
far too small for it.

61
00:04:31,006 --> 00:04:32,207
Next, a third drawer.

62
00:04:32,207 --> 00:04:35,294
Instead of describing where, I sketch it with Mark up:

63
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:38,096
under the other two, and all the way to the back.

64
00:04:39,046 --> 00:04:43,176
A rectangle under the drawers, an arrow from the front to the back, and a few words.

65
00:04:50,072 --> 00:04:52,683
Send it to SOMA AI, and add one sentence:

66
00:04:52,683 --> 00:04:55,040
the pen cup should stay just as deep.

67
00:04:59,273 --> 00:05:03,000
SOMA AI adds a drawer underneath, as deep as the whole organizer.

68
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,243
It lifts the pen cup with everything above, so the cup stays just as deep.

69
00:05:08,193 --> 00:05:09,756
Now there are three drawers.

70
00:05:09,756 --> 00:05:14,723
The organizer is 25 millimeters taller, and the cards still fit in the two upper drawers.

71
00:05:15,673 --> 00:05:17,699
A cut through the side shows it best:

72
00:05:17,699 --> 00:05:21,147
the new drawer runs all the way to the back, under the pen cup.

73
00:05:21,147 --> 00:05:23,392
And the cup is still 90 millimeters deep.

74
00:05:32,273 --> 00:05:36,563
To compare the two, I ask SOMA AI to put the original next to the new organizer.

75
00:05:42,373 --> 00:05:45,622
It moves the original over, with a gap and the fronts lined up.

76
00:05:46,572 --> 00:05:47,320
Side by side:

77
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:50,483
the download on the left, and our version on the right.

78
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:56,062
Wider, a bit taller, with room for business cards, and a third drawer that goes all the way back.

79
00:05:57,305 --> 00:05:58,523
Finally, Export.

80
00:05:58,523 --> 00:06:00,578
3MF or STL for your slicer:

81
00:06:00,578 --> 00:06:04,155
the body and all three drawers, ready to print.

82
00:06:05,838 --> 00:06:09,888
If you share your remix, credit the original author and keep the same license.

83
00:06:11,938 --> 00:06:18,143
From a download that didn't fit my needs to a model I can change in plain words, without drawing a single line.

84
00:06:18,143 --> 00:06:19,988
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app.
